{
 "slug": "js_typed_methods",
 "course": "js",
 "order": 242,
 "url": "/js/js_typed_methods.asp",
 "title": "Typed Array Methods",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "Typed Array Methods"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The from() Method"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The from()method creates a new typed array from any iterable object:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const myArr = Int16Array.from(\"1234567890\");",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const myArr = Int16Array.from([1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,0]);",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_typed_from_string"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The of() Method"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The of() method creates a new typed array from a number of arguments:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const myArr = Int16Array.of(1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,0);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_typed_of"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The constructor.name Property"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The constructor.name property returns the name (type) of a typed array:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "myArr.constructor.name",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_typed_name"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The BYTES_PER_ELEMENT Property"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "BYTES_PER_ELEMENT returns the number of bytes used to store each array element:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "myArr.BYTES_PER_ELEMENT",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_typed_bytes"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Common Array Methods"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Typed Arrays share many methods with Standard Arrays:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Iteration: forEach(), map(), filter(), reduce(), reduceRight(), every(), some(), find(),\nfindIndex(), findLast(), findLastIndex().",
    "Searching: includes(), indexOf(), lastIndexOf().",
    "Manipulation: at(), copyWithin(), fill(), reverse(), set(), slice(), sort(), subarray().",
    "Conversion: join(), toLocaleString(), toString().",
    "Non-mutating methods: toReversed(), toSorted(), with()."
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The fill() Method"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The fill() method changes all elements in a typed array to a value:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "myArr.fill(200);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_typed_fill"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The fill() method takes two optional arguments: start index and end index:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "myArr.fill(200, 0, 3);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_typed_fill_some"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The find() Method"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The find() method returns the first element that satisfies a test:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "myArr.find((x) => x > 18)",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_typed_find"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The some() Method"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The some() method returns true if an element for which a provided function returns true:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "myArr.some((x) => x > 18)",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_typed_some"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Not Available Array Methods"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Some array methods are NOT available for typed array."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "This is due to the fixed-length nature and the lack of fixed structure."
  },
